Before I write the code, a few questions:

1. Where should the new command live?
   - a) In `extend-template.ts`, registered by the existing `registerExtendTemplateCommand`, sharing the existing helpers (recommended, since it is a variant of the same command)
   - b) In a new file `extend-template-named.ts` with its own `registerExtendTemplateNamedCommand`, with the shared helpers exported from `extend-template.ts`

2. How should the sequence number work when named files exist?
   - a) Shared counter. If `example-2026-10-24-0003.convo` or `example-2026-10-24-0003-other.convo` exists, the next file gets `0004` (recommended, avoids duplicate numbers)
   - b) Only check whether the exact path exists, so `0003-some_name` could coexist with `0003`

3. Suppose the source file already has a name suffix, such as `example-2026-10-24-0003-some_name.convo`, and has no `!template` imports. How should the base name be derived?
   - a) Strip both the date/number and the name suffix, so the base is `example` (recommended)
   - b) Strip only the date/number pattern, and treat anything that does not match as part of the base name

4. What should happen if the user submits an empty name? (Pressing Escape will always cancel.)
   - a) Cancel the command
   - b) Create the file without a name suffix, the same as `convo.extend-template`
   - c) Show a validation error in the input box until a non-empty name is entered

5. Should the input be trimmed before sanitizing, so that `" some name "` becomes `some_name` rather than `_some_name_`?
   - a) Yes, trim first (recommended)
   - b) No, sanitize the raw input

6. Should the command be added to the editor title menu as well?
   - a) No, only the command palette and the keybinding
   - b) Yes, add it next to the existing Extend Template button, using a different icon


